    "project": "Lang",
    "summary": "[lang] DateUtils.truncate method is buggy when dealing with DST switching hours",
    "description": "Try to truncate 2004-10-31 01:00:00 MDT by hour and you'll actually get 2004-10-\n\n31 01:00:00 MST, which is one hour after the input hour.\n\n// truncate 2004-10-31 01:00:00 MDT\n\nDate oct31_01MDT = new Date(1099206000000L); \n\nDate result = DateUtils.truncate(oct31_01MDT, Calendar.HOUR_OF_DAY);\n\nassertEquals(oct31_01MDT, result);"
  },
